# Cloudflare Pages rules for the Sang app marketing site, which now owns the apex
# (https://www.sangapp.in/). Rules are evaluated top to bottom and the first match wins.
#
# IMPORTANT: on Pages these rules run BEFORE static-asset lookup, so a catch-all
# `/*  /  200` would swallow /assets/*, /logo.png, /robots.txt and friends and hand back
# the HTML shell for all of them. Never add a bare `/*` rule here. Unknown paths already
# fall back to index.html on their own, so the catch-all buys nothing anyway.
#
# Static rules are listed before the splat rule: Pages matches them faster, and a splat
# must not shadow a more specific path (/app/privacy vs /app/*).

# Legacy paths. This site used to live under /app while the Event CRM owned "/", so store
# listings and old inbound links still point at /app and /app/privacy.
/app             /          301
/app/            /          301
/app/privacy     /privacy   301
/app/privacy/    /privacy   301

# Client-side routes (react-router BrowserRouter). Rewriting to "/index.html" is rejected
# by Pages as an infinite loop (it strips "/index" and re-matches this rule), so rewrite to
# the DIRECTORY "/" instead: already normalized, so it serves index.html with a 200 and the
# URL is preserved for the router. Add a line here for every new route the site gains.
/privacy         /          200

# Anything else still under the old /app prefix goes home.
/app/*           /          301
